From 012ea9b3558755628575925d1efc8c7838fe94b0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: lccc-v14 <v14@localhost>
Date: Fri, 14 Aug 2026 08:33:10 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/4] PGO: hot loop-header alignment + fix single-function
 profile gate + assembler defects
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Three defects fixed and one flagship feature, all driven by -fprofile-use:

1. summary::has_spread wrongly treated a SINGLE-function profile as flat:
   the 'max >= 2*second_max.max(1)' clamp required max >= 2 when second_max
   was 0, gating out single-function units whose entry function runs once
   (the common benchmark shape). Their hot loops never got layout/alignment/
   unroll decisions despite carrying all the count. A lone hot function is the
   OPPOSITE of the v10 tied-hot-functions flat-profile case; fix: second_max
   == 0 -> spread is trivially true.

2. Profile-driven hot loop-header + hot join-point alignment (the
   -falign-loops / -falign-labels transform; LLVM -align-loops, Intel 2.6.2).
   layout computes, from the derived profile, hot loop headers (backedge
   targets with >= 1/16 of entry count) and hot join points (in-degree >= 2),
   and codegen emits .p2align 4 (16-byte, 32 for very hot large-body loops)
   before them. Gated on has_spread so cold code never bloats.

3. x86 assembler jump relaxation made TWO-DIRECTIONAL: jumps start long and
   shrink when the displacement fits a signed byte, but the old long->short
   -only loop left a short jump short when alignment padding pushed its
   target out of range, truncating the displacement ('as i8' wrap) and
   branching into the MIDDLE of an instruction (SIGSEGV inside movabs —
   exposed by the .p2align padding). Jumps now grow back to long when
   needed (can_grow), and the final displacement patch asserts range.

4. fixup_alignment_markers never updated the marker's padding after
   adjusting it, so the next fixup pass (relax_jumps iterates; emit_elf runs
   a final pass) re-applied the same stale adjustment and drained past the
   section end (panic 'range end index out of range'). Fixed to record the
   post-fixup padding, making the pass idempotent.

Validated: regression 144 passed / 0 failed, correctness 50/50, intrinsics
3/3; loopbench PGO binary bit-identical to plain and hot loop header
16-byte aligned.
