The alignment feature was gated on summary::has_spread (cross-function
dominance), which a tied-hot profile [3x1.2M, 10x40K] fails — withholding the
safe loop-header alignment win. Alignment is a fundamentally cheaper and safer
transform than the PGO inliner (a few NOP bytes on a block executed >= 1/16 of
the function entry, never a control-flow/inlining change), so it is now gated
on the per-block hotness check alone.

New pgo_sections roundtrip test: a skewed dispatcher (3 hot + 10 cold handlers
+ a hot loop) verified end-to-end — .text.hot contains the hot trio,
.text.unlikely the cold handlers, and .p2align appears before the hot loop
header, with bit-identical output.
