+
+## PGO redesign (v14): defects fixed + hot-loop alignment + sectioning
+
+Five defects fixed and two features added, all profile-driven:
+
+1. **has_spread wrongly gated single-function profiles.** The `max >= 2*second_max.max(1)` dominance check required `max >= 2` when `second_max == 0`, so a unit whose only function runs ONCE was treated as "flat" and its hot loops never got layout/alignment/unroll decisions. A lone function is the maximally-SKEWED case (the opposite of the v10 tied-hot-flat regression it guards); `second_max == 0 -> true`.
+
+2. **x86 assembler jump relaxation was long->short only.** A short jump whose target got pushed out of ±127 by (newly possible) .p2align padding kept its wrapped `as i8` displacement and branched into the MIDDLE of an instruction (SIGSEGV inside `movabs`). Relaxation is now two-directional (jumps grow back to long via `can_grow`), and the final short-displacement patch asserts range.
+
+3. **fixup_alignment_markers was not idempotent.** It never recorded the post-fixup padding, so the next pass re-applied the same stale adjustment and drained past the section end (assembler panic, `range end index out of range`) — latent because `.text` never carried align markers before. Now records the new padding; the pass converges.
+
+4. **Hot/cold section classification collapsed on skewed units.** The 90%-percentile threshold landed at the tail count for [3x1.2M, 10x40K, 1], classifying the 1%-execution helpers as hot and stuffing .text.hot with cold code. Section placement now uses a dedicated ratio (hot = >=10% of the unit's hottest function; cold = <0.1% of it); inlining keeps the percentile thresholds (their aggressiveness is correct there).
+
+5. **Single-block functions were never sectioned.** `layout_module` skipped functions with <2 blocks, so a unit of tiny cold helpers polluted .text. Whole-function section classification now applies to every function; only intra-function layout needs >=2 blocks.
+
+Features:
+- **Hot loop-header + hot join-point alignment** (`.p2align 4`, 32-byte for very hot large-body loops) from the derived profile — the `-falign-loops`/`-align-labels` transform lccc's main backend lacked. Gated on per-block hotness (>= 1/16 of entry count), so cold code never pads.
+- **`pgo_sections` roundtrip test** pins the whole chain end-to-end (hot/cold split + .p2align + bit-identical output).
+
+Validated: regression 144/144, correctness 50/50, intrinsics 3/3, 597 lib
+tests, PGO roundtrip script (incl. new sections+alignment stage), corpus
+perf-neutral. The assembler relaxation fixes benefit EVERY binary, not just
+PGO builds.
